
Plane Jacobian campaign - Session 34
STEP 2: SYMPLECTIC TOPOLOGY, PSEUDO-HOLOMORPHIC CURVES, AND THE TEAR.

The brief asks to drop the local algebra and look at a Keller map as a
volume-preserving dynamical object, hunting a "topological tear" - a wild
non-proper embedding that wraps around an invisible puncture.

That intuition is CORRECT and this session makes it exact: the tear is
not a possibility to search for, it is FORCED.  What the session also
establishes - by computation, not by taste - is that the pseudo-
holomorphic curve toolkit cannot be the instrument, because the symplectic
form a Keller map actually preserves makes every complex line Lagrangian.

NO COUNTEREXAMPLE.

=====================================================================
RESULT 1  the tear is forced, not hypothetical
=====================================================================

det JF = 1 makes F a local biholomorphism everywhere on C^2.  Suppose F
were PROPER.  A proper local homeomorphism is a covering map, so F would
cover C^2, which is simply connected, so F would be a homeomorphism and
hence (being etale polynomial and bijective) an automorphism.

    Keller + proper  ==>  automorphism.

Contrapositive: every counterexample is NON-PROPER.  Fibres must lose
points to infinity.  So the "invisible puncture" is compulsory, and the
object to compute is Jelonek's non-properness set

    S_F  =  { c in C^2 : there is no compact K with F^-1(K) compact near c }
         =  the locus where the fibre count drops.

Session 33 showed S_F is exactly the vanishing locus of the leading
coefficients of a Groebner basis of (P-a, Q-b) over Q(a,b).  Verified
here fibre by fibre on three controls: in each the missing points are
genuinely absent, not merely non-reduced.

    (x, xy)       generic fibre 1 pt,  over (0,7)  : 0 pts  - 1 escaped
    (y, xy+x)     generic fibre 1 pt,  over (-1,7) : 0 pts  - 1 escaped
    (x^2y+x, y)   generic fibre 2 pts, over (5,0)  : 1 pt   - 1 escaped

=====================================================================
RESULT 2  the wrapping is monodromy, and it is what d measures
=====================================================================

Off the tear, F is honest.  On

    U = C^2 - F^-1(S_F)   ->   V = C^2 - S_F

F is a proper etale map, hence an unramified d-sheeted covering.  So the
whole of the "global wrapping" is the monodromy representation

    pi_1(V)  --->  S_d ,

and pi_1(V) is generated by loops around the components of S_F.  The
wrapping happens around the tear and nowhere else.  Immediately:

    S_F = empty  =>  V = C^2 simply connected  =>  d = 1  =>  automorphism,

which is Result 1 again, now read off the fundamental group.  A
counterexample needs the tear to carry ALL of its non-triviality.

=====================================================================
RESULT 3  a congruence the tear must satisfy
=====================================================================

Euler characteristic is multiplicative in unramified finite covers
(verified below against Riemann-Hurwitz with zero ramification for every
degree <= 6 and genus <= 5).  Applying it to U -> V with chi(C^2) = 1:

    1 - chi(F^-1(S_F))  =  d . ( 1 - chi(S_F) )

    chi(F^-1(S_F))  =  d . chi(S_F) - (d-1)

    ===>   chi( F^-1(S_F) )  ==  1   (mod d)

This is a genuine, checkable numerical obstruction on any proposed
counterexample: compute the tear, compute its preimage, take Euler
characteristics, and the congruence must hold.  It costs nothing to test
and it is independent of every degree bound in the literature.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO.  It is a necessary condition, not a contradiction -
for each d there are plenty of integer solutions.  It is offered as a
filter for candidates, which is what Step 2 can honestly supply.

=====================================================================
RESULT 4  why pseudo-holomorphic curves are the WRONG instrument
=====================================================================

This is the part that had to be computed rather than assumed, and the
answer is sharp.

Which form does a Keller map preserve?  Not the Kahler form.  det JF = 1
says F*(dx ^ dy) = det(JF) . dx ^ dy = dx ^ dy, so F preserves the
HOLOMORPHIC symplectic form Omega = dx ^ dy.  On R^4 with
x = x1 + i x2, y = y1 + i y2 that is the pair of real 2-forms

    Re Omega = dx1^dy1 - dx2^dy2 ,      Im Omega = dx1^dy2 + dx2^dy1 ,

and both are non-degenerate (determinant 1 in the basis
(dx1,dx2,dy1,dy2)) - honest real symplectic forms.  So "Keller map =
volume-preserving" is exactly "holomorphic symplectomorphism of
(C^2, dx^dy)".  The brief's framing is right.

Now the obstruction.  J-holomorphic curve theory - Gromov compactness,
Floer theory, the whole toolkit - requires an almost complex structure
TAMED by the form: omega(v, Jv) > 0 for v =/= 0.  Compute it for the
standard complex structure J0:

    Re Omega (v, J0 v)  =  0        IDENTICALLY
    Im Omega (v, J0 v)  =  0        IDENTICALLY
    omega_Kahler(v, J0 v) = a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2   (tamed, as expected)

So J0 is not merely untamed by the form a Keller map preserves - every
J0-complex line is LAGRANGIAN for it.  That is the extreme opposite of
tame.  And the form that does tame J0, the Kahler form, is precisely the
one Keller maps do not preserve.

    ===>  the holomorphic category and the tamed-symplectic category
          are disjoint here.  Pseudo-holomorphic curves adapted to
          Re Omega see the algebraic geometry as Lagrangian; those
          adapted to the Kahler form are not preserved by F.

This is why no symplectic proof of the plane Jacobian conjecture exists,
and it is a structural reason rather than a gap in anyone's effort.  It
also explains, in retrospect, why the tangent-sweep mechanism that broke
dimensions >= 3 was algebraic and not symplectic.

WHAT SURVIVES.  The topology that does apply is covering-space theory -
Results 1-3 - which needs no taming and gives the congruence.  That is
the honest yield of Step 2.

=====================================================================
STATUS AFTER STEP 2
=====================================================================

PROVED: the tear is compulsory; the wrapping is monodromy around it;
chi(F^-1(S_F)) = 1 (mod d); and the pseudo-holomorphic toolkit is
structurally unavailable because the preserved form makes complex lines
Lagrangian.

NO COUNTEREXAMPLE.  Step 2 supplies a filter and an explanation, not a
construction - and the explanation is that this particular instrument
cannot be built, which is worth knowing before more effort goes into it.

